{"page": 9, "text": "Revenue by Product Categories In the first quarter of Fiscal 2027, as part of the Company\u2019s enterprise assessment, we reclassified certain products and disclosed an additional product category, Portfolio. The Portfolio category represents mature, non-core products that are primarily on-premise solutions, that we continue to provide maintenance and support services. The Company believes this presentation provides additional information regarding how management views revenue by product category. As a result of these changes, the Company\u2019s data management solutions are now reported within eight product categories: Content, Business Network, IT Operations Management (ITOM), Cybersecurity (Enterprise), Cybersecurity (Small and Medium-Sized Businesses (SMB) & Consumer), Application Delivery Management (ADM), Analytics, and Portfolio. In addition, certain products were reclassified from the Cybersecurity (Enterprise) product category to the Cybersecurity (SMB & Consumer) product category. Historical revenues related to the eDOCS business, which was divested in Fiscal 2026, and previously included in Analytics, were reclassified to the Portfolio product category. Prior period amounts have been reclassified to conform to the current period presentation. These reclassifications affected only the presentation of revenue by product category and had no impact on previously reported consolidated revenue, operating income, net income, earnings per share, or cash flows. The following table disaggregates total revenue and total cloud services and subscription revenue by product category for the periods indicated:\nThree Months Ended September 30,\n2026 2025\nTotal Revenues by Product Categories\nContent $ 523,010 $ 477,874\nBusiness Network 160,894 160,501\nITOM 84,734 96,604\nCybersecurity (Enterprise) 95,830 109,337\nCybersecurity (SMB & Consumer) 127,717 140,189\nADM 103,970 120,911\nAnalytics 20,721 40,760\nPortfolio 119,758 141,959\nTotal revenues