{"page": 63, "text": "Three Months Ended September 30, 2026 Compared to Three Months Ended September 30, 2025 Cloud services and subscriptions revenues increased by $21.0 million or 4.3% during the three months ended September 30, 2026, as compared to the same period in the prior fiscal year; up 4.3% after excluding the unfavourable impact of $0.1 million of foreign exchange rate changes. The change was primarily driven by increases in the Content, Business Network, ITOM, Cybersecurity (Enterprise) and Analytics product categories, partly offset by a decrease in the Cybersecurity (SMB & Consumer), ADM and Portfolio product categories. Geographically, the overall change was attributable to an increase in EMEA of $17.1 million, an increase in Asia Pacific of $2.8 million and an increase in Americas of $1.1 million. There were 35 cloud services contracts greater than $1.0 million that closed during the first quarter of Fiscal 2027, compared to 33 contracts during the first quarter of Fiscal 2026. Cost of Cloud services and subscriptions revenues increased by $6.2 million during the three months ended September 30, 2026, as compared to the same period in the prior fiscal year. This was primarily due to an increase in third-party network usage fees of $3.4 million and an increase in labour-related costs of $2.3 million. Overall, the gross margin percentage on Cloud services and subscriptions revenues increased to 65% from 64%. 2) Client Support: Client support revenues consist of revenues from our client support and maintenance agreements. These agreements allow our clients to receive technical support, enhancements and upgrades to new versions of our software products when available. Client support revenues are generated from support and maintenance relating to current year sales of software products and from the renewal of existing maintenance agreements for software licenses sold in prior periods. Therefore, changes in Client support revenues do not always correlate directly to the changes in license revenues from period to period. The terms of support and maintenance agreements are typically twelve months, and are renewable, generally on an annual basis, at the option of the client. Our management reviews our client support renewal rates on a quarterly basis, and we use these rates as a method of monitoring our client service performance. For the quarter ended September 30, 2026, our client support net renewal rate (Client Support NRR) increased to 92%, as compared to 91% for the quarter ended September 30, 2025. Client Support NRR measures the percentage of annual contract value retained from Enterprise client support agreements available to renew, after giving effect to contract expansions (such as price increases and upsells) and reductions (cancellations). Client Support NRR excludes internal portfolio movements (such as migrations to the Company's Cloud and other offerings). Client Support NRR includes enterprise-based clients, which contribute approximately 90%\n"}
